+# Production wrapper V2: source/CPU repair, unreleased
+
+Base V1 24-file inventory `192d4d7dbf04f938cc47c2171a05240a014bf676b195a09116af97fb2908e742` and its independent rejection `a0682eeebcef5a762b2c2fd5eeafe767d0e6d2c3013cd2520244a03406498507` remain immutable. V2 is an independent directory; source f7e, zero wrappers, assets and jobs are unchanged.
+
+## P01/P02 own scheduler identity
+
+`slurm_identity.py` queries only the default controller with controlled environment and `scontrol --local`, requires exactly `ClusterName=wuhan-h100` and no federation, and parses unique actual allocation tokens: numeric JobId, exact h100-9 NodeList/BatchHost, one node, exclusive 8GPU, task32CPU, memory256G, 72h, requeue0 and restart0. Actual allocated CPUs may exceed32 under exclusive reservation and are reported separately. A foreign runtime cluster declaration is refused. Launch and supervisor both verify this tuple; supervisor preserves raw configuration/federation/allocation, own run/manifest/review binding and names of removed routing variables.
+
+`submit_once.py` is now a concrete reviewed candidate, not an absent external implementation. It requires the whole-package first-five release, exact source/renderer pins and exact derived script bytes, rechecks local queue and cluster-qualified prior terminal accounting, takes an ordinary no-follow dispatch lock, and durably creates the new intent before its sole injected/default submission call. Foreign suffixes or unknown results preserve UNKNOWN and never retry; legacy journals missing cluster block. Initial and final journal file/directory fsync, atomic replacement and exact timeout-byte preservation are implemented. No actual scheduler executable was run in development. Runtime lineage consumes the original submit's cluster proof and successful exact stdout along with numeric JobID, node, run and manifest/review pins. No `-M` route is used.
+
+`guard_entry.py` executes the exact original guard bytes as their actual top-level argparse/while-loop script, with original argv installed before execution. It independently revalidates the same tuple and controls subprocess environment. The original unbound bare-ID `scancel` is always refused with retained JSON; no scheduler cancellation is issued. The original STOP/dual15% decision remains effective: the guard exits nonzero and the supervisor's original cgroup-owned cleanup terminates only this allocation's owned children, then the batch exits. Unknown/foreign lineage cannot cancel anything. External resource guard, original eight background PID starts, UUID leases and numerical MEM/SM limits are unchanged. This fallback must be verified on the real owned runtime; local tests do not prove GPU/process coexistence.
+
+The final release binds renderer/submitter source and manifest rather than its own generated script SHA, preventing a release-SHA/script-SHA cycle. The exact script is deterministically rendered from final release pins and its actual SHA/bytes are retained in the once journal.
+
+## P03 staged unchanged thresholds
+
+Prelaunch `threshold_acceptance` is now only `INDEPENDENT_FRESH200_MU_BOOTSTRAP_THRESHOLDS_ACCEPTED`: first credited outers1..5, fullrun/6..200 acceptance false, KL0.2 from the latest human goal, tail/repeat candidates bound to all eight actual zero monitor SHA and numeric observations. Historical zero-only `PRODUCTION_THRESHOLDS_ACCEPTED` receipts are refused. The whole-package release status is `READY_FOR_FRESH200_BEHAVIOR_MU_FIRST5_BOOTSTRAP`; no fullrun threshold acceptance exists before short training.
+
+The live gate envelope must include an independently authored `threshold_assessment` path/SHA. The same-job/run/source/config review binds it, partial raw CPU report and the original first5 proof. Assessment status is `INDEPENDENT_SAME_INSTANCE_FIRST5_THRESHOLDS_ACCEPTED`, exact first5/continue6..200, zero ready/review and bootstrap SHA, unchanged values, nonempty explicit rationale, and exact measured all-attempt/all-rank safety JSON SHA/metrics/counts/refusals. The wrapper rereads actual safety decisions/configs; absent monitor metrics/records or drift cannot become empty-string/boolean acceptance. It publishes only external review bytes to approved.json, fsyncs the directory, and records assessment SHA. Final verification rereads the same short-training assessment and review. No parameter value is changed at the gate and no second training instance is used.
+
+## P04 retained partial bytes and logical state
+
+Both attempt/checkpoint accounting now physically reread all eight worker snapshots, driver and actor-input files for every historical partial. `partial_raw_evidence.py` holds every directory component and ordinary file via no-follow openat, stream-hashes the same FD, checks path/inode/stat stability and source-recorded sizes (driver size only when actually present). Exact attempt directory, rank and context are required. The hashes join independent proof bindings.
+
+The added fourth serial same-node CPU checker `check_partial_raw_cpu.py` loads every retained raw state from that same SHA-bound FD only on Linux h100-9 with CUDA empty, and verifies source-native logical digest/identity, all20 opportunity ledger and actual calls/scheduler, sampler consumed attempt/RNG/accounting and actor context/rows. It requires model/Adam/scheduler finite while preserving and separately reporting raw NaN gradients; it never restores/rolls back a worker. Empty histories explicitly mean0 files/0 PT loads. `CpuChecks.proofs` rechecks physical mappings and exact10×partial coverage/deserialization before accepting the CPU report; external first5 review and threshold assessment must bind that report. Final repeats the full history.
+
+Local fixtures use only tiny ordinary non-PT bytes and pure logical dictionaries. Real official/raw PT/model/tokenizer, CUDA/FSDP/Ray, optimizer and Slurm were not executed. Same-node real IO/logical reload is still unperformed; exact restart/resume remains false.
+
+## Evidence and current blockers
+
+The existing f7 none-context source/CPU receipt `6f2ceaebd1ff6c04e9330b404e17ff7db9df7493db5c686cbc3366cb3253fb44` is actual source evidence only. It is not V2 package permission, actual zero acceptance or production threshold acceptance. Every missing production metadata descriptor stays null. Actual zero/tokenizer preflight, bootstrap observation authority, V2 none-context review, frozen package/dispatch proof, same-node resources, first5 external review and short threshold assessment, final evaluation and independent effects remain required/unaccepted.
+
+Owner CPU logs preserve first command/cwd/fixture failures and affected reruns. V2 owner evidence is not an independent release. No original mathematical loss/Tree weighting/sampler configuration/cadence/count/budget was changed.
